"sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"28df3902faea76becbcdd79d644371c27522635f39d7fdc164096bf3f7b4a956","compact":"50748b54bd0f4fbfd39fe9939728f454243eef40f7dbbeb70cef074771f7c106","nasal":"92085cdd7b317257693ecf2eaabe804942e33eb51cde9a1ca8c3887c884cbf17"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-39-12","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":39,"verse":12,"english":"And that best of men, Räma, will soon be installed in the kingdom, in company with these three, the Earth, Vaidehī, and the goddess of victory.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.879,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-44-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2039012","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"664ace140e0213a118c8cf39d4edc0fd4359724bd80ae6b7655cacd464789114","compact":"47aacc748d54828fc75a18cd1bb22c11ad08e263c23b4a2601646205d1784522","nasal":"47aacc748d54828fc75a18cd1bb22c11ad08e263c23b4a2601646205d1784522"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-39-13","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":39,"verse":13,"english":"And again seeing him returned and crowned with great auspiciousness, you will speedily shed the dew of delight.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.309,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-44-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2039013","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ccdeee2d08b60c759dac7533a80b050c7611b56a7bc7df3502e806763cd9e0c6","compact":"21463c4a6823c9fc78a3fa366cdb218cb5553e09a8b156ff821c3e84ce796409","nasal":"b255b8abf934dcd02469ddb6e99ab39a6af8cec7e0429473099705f658aa1cbe"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-39-14","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":39,"verse":14,"english":"Beholding your son surrounded by his friends, bowing to you, you will soon shed blissful tears, even like a rain-cloud.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.806,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-44-23"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2039014","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"be6c3d328b838cad3febadbe4688f0a9d25fe2e46fde4351abc390c39b31cd23","compact":"0ebe45a28daf19d349c8be75d9996530f9e7b45bfaf324acc65ca322a80be9f3","nasal":"0352580fc6a45b0a1ebb44bfb2bfceed26ebbfc1f45821c3e05ac4b007aa0e65"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-39-15","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":39,"verse":15,"english":"And soon will your son conferring boons, returning (to this place), press your feet with those soft and plump hands of his.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-44-24"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2039015","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"78ce42e19efcc866a9c67b333f5175f4493e8ab3def65761675eb360c58bf3a0","compact":"db55adf27c48e1ef830d9e8cfe2524f750cc15ce6c0b286f7947b708009f5a60","nasal":"db55adf27c48e1ef830d9e8cfe2524f750cc15ce6c0b286f7947b708009f5a60"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-39-16","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":39,"verse":16,"english":"Hearing those words of Laksmana's mother, the wife of the best of men, Rāma's mother, had her sorrow destroyed in her person, even like and autumnal cloud surcharged with slight rain.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.905,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-44-27"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2039016","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b604363087c47f0a7b01f44bc14a7a3aeee039193d150161fd24bdd0b0232f06","compact":"f7a0354b7bd7affed8987781aed0d49cb87286ce55f4b6aec72ea8dfe1c1400d","nasal":"f7a0354b7bd7affed8987781aed0d49cb87286ce55f4b6aec72ea8dfe1c1400d"}}]
